---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const updated = '7 November 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Qivy"
  description="What Qivy does and does not collect. A static site with no analytics, no cookies set by us, no accounts and no newsletter signup."
>
  <section class="hdr wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy' }]} />
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap body">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This page describes what actually happens when you visit qivy.in. It is
        written to match how the site is currently built, not as boilerplate.
        If that changes, this page changes with it.
      </p>

      <h2>What Qivy collects</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Nothing, directly.</strong> Qivy is a static website. There are
        no accounts, no logins, no comment system, no newsletter signup form,
        no contact form and no advertising. There is nothing here that asks you
        for personal information, so there is nothing for this site to store.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <p>Qivy sets no cookies.</p>
      <p>
        One item is stored in your browser's <strong>local storage</strong>: a
        key named <code>qivy-theme</code>, holding either <code>dark</code> or
        <code>light</code>. It exists only so the site remembers your theme
        choice between visits. It is never sent anywhere, contains no
        identifier, and clearing your browser data removes it.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>No analytics are currently installed.</strong> No page-view
        tracking, no heatmaps, no session recording, no third-party tracking
        scripts of any kind.
      </p>
      <p>
        If analytics are added later, a privacy-respecting and cookie-free
        option will be used, and this page will be updated to name it before it
        goes live.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties that do see something</h2>
      <p>Two services are involved in delivering this site to you:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> hosts the site. Like any web host,
          GitHub receives the network request for each page — which includes
          your IP address and browser user-agent — in order to serve it. This
          is handled under
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Fonts</strong> serves the two typefaces this site
          uses. Your browser requests those font files from Google's servers,
          which means Google receives that request. This is covered by
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Neither is a tracking arrangement set up by Qivy — they are a
        consequence of where the site is hosted and where its fonts come from.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Articles link out to documentation, tools and vendor websites. Those
        sites have their own privacy practices, and Qivy has no control over
        and no insight into what they collect.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Qivy is a general technology publication and is not directed at
        children. Since it collects no personal information from anyone, it
        collects none from children either.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Data-protection rights — access, correction, deletion, portability —
        apply to personal data a site holds about you. Qivy holds none, so
        there is nothing to request, correct or delete. If analytics or a
        newsletter are added in future, this section will be updated to
        explain how to exercise those rights.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        Any change to this policy will be reflected in the "last updated" date
        above. Because this site is version-controlled in public, the full
        history of changes to this page is visible in its
        <a href="https://github.com/fshbet/qivy-site" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">repository</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can go to
        <a href="https://github.com/fshbet" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/fshbet</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hdr {
    padding-block: var(--sp-6);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bd);
  }
  h1 {
    margin-top: var(--sp-5);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
  }
  .meta {
    margin-top: var(--sp-3);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    color: var(--text-3);
  }
  .body {
    padding-top: var(--sp-7);
  }
</style>
